adrnext_* -- the fixtures for `kuna xrefs` over an address that is the
instruction right after the one forming it (GH #1360), and over the return
address every kind of link leaves, which is never a reference
(decompiler/crates/kuna-cli/tests/xrefs_cli.rs).

What they are
  adrnext_aarch64      static AArch64 ELF: adr to itself, to the next and to
                       the one after next; bl, blr and a bl to the next.
  adrnext_macho_arm64  arm64 Mach-O dylib from the issue's own assembly.
  adrnext_x86_64       static x86-64 ELF: lea rax,[rip] and mov eax,offset to
                       the next instruction; call, call *, call $+5, syscall.
  adrnext_arm          static A32/Thumb-2 ELF: adr and adr.w to the next
                       instruction; bl, blx, mov lr,pc + bx, a bl to the next.
  adrnext_rv64         static RV64 ELF: auipc + addi ending right before the
                       label it forms; call, jalr ra, jal t0, a jal to the next.
  adrnext_ppc32        static PPC32 ELF: bcl 20,31 and bl to the next, bl, bctrl.
  adrnext_mips         static MIPS32 BE ELF: bal past its delay slot, bltzal
                       $zero (SLEIGH's nal), jal, jalr.
  adrnext_mips64       static MIPS64 BE (n64) ELF, the same four links; read
                       with --target MIPS:BE:64:default.
  adrnext_sh4          synthetic static SuperH-4 LE ELF: mova to the next
                       address alone and in the delay slot of rts and bt/s;
                       bsr. Read with --target SuperH4:LE:32:default.
  Sources: adrnext_<arch>.S, adrnext_macho.s, adrnext_sh4.py.

Why they are vendored
  They are assembled and linked for seven foreign targets, which CI has no
  toolchain for; the SuperH one is generated so its bytes stay fixed.

Where they came from
  Ubuntu clang 14.0.0 assembles; LLD 23.1.4 (docker image mstorsjo/llvm-mingw)
  links the ELFs, and the rustup-bundled ld64.lld (LLD 20.1.8, rustc 1.90.0)
  the Mach-O:

      clang -target aarch64-linux-gnu -c adrnext_aarch64.S -o aarch64.o
      clang -target x86_64-linux-gnu -c adrnext_x86_64.S -o x86_64.o
      clang -target armv7a-linux-gnueabi -c adrnext_arm.S -o arm.o
      clang -target riscv64-linux-gnu -c adrnext_rv64.S -o rv64.o
      clang -target powerpc-linux-gnu -c adrnext_ppc32.S -o ppc32.o
      clang -target mips-linux-gnu -mno-abicalls -fno-pic -c adrnext_mips.S -o mips.o
      clang -target mips64-linux-gnuabi64 -mno-abicalls -fno-pic -c adrnext_mips64.S -o mips64.o
      ld.lld -static -nostdlib -e main --build-id=none --no-relax <arch>.o \
          -o adrnext_<arch>
      clang -target arm64-apple-macos11 -c adrnext_macho.s -o macho.o
      ld64.lld -dylib -arch arm64 -platform_version macos 11.0 11.0 \
          -o adrnext_macho_arm64 macho.o
      python3 adrnext_sh4.py

